stdlib.module.std::ffi::c
std::ffi::c -- standard namespace
Indices: stdlib

SUMMARY
    The C ABI value universe: target-sized C integer types, and affine C
    pointers with null, null?, clone, erase and retype.

SYMBOL
    std::ffi::c

DESCRIPTION
    These are the values a C boundary carries, modeled as C's ABI sees them, not
    as C's source language spells them. Nothing here calls C: C calls are
    `extern c fn` declarations (C-FFI.md), and C calling Botlish back is a
    `callback c fn` (C-CALLBACK-MILESTONE-1.md, below).

    C integer scalars (intrinsic types of this namespace):

      std::ffi::c::Char std::ffi::c::SChar std::ffi::c::UChar std::ffi::c::Short std::ffi::c::UShort
      std::ffi::c::Int std::ffi::c::UInt std::ffi::c::Long std::ffi::c::ULong
      std::ffi::c::LongLong std::ffi::c::ULongLong

    Each is an integer domain: its values are ordinary Ints in exactly the
    compilation's C target's range of that C type (`-target`, the host's by
    default: std::ffi::c::Long is Int in -2^63..2^63-1 on linux-x86_64 and
    -2^31..2^31-1 on windows-x86_64; std::ffi::c::Char is signed or unsigned as
    the target's plain char is). Arithmetic on them is Botlish arithmetic (no C
    promotion, no wrapping); an Int becomes one only where its range proves it
    fits. std::ffi::c::Int and std::ffi::c::Long stay two types where their
    ranges agree.

    C floating types (intrinsic types of this namespace,
    C-FLOAT-FFI-MILESTONE-1.md): C representations whose values are Float64s.

      std::ffi::c::Double       C's double, IEEE 754 binary64 (8 bytes): every
                                Float64 is one, exactly
      std::ffi::c::Float        C's float, IEEE 754 binary32 (4 bytes): a
                                Float64 leaving for one is rounded to nearest,
                                ties to even, and one that rounds to an
                                infinity is NonFiniteFloat before C runs (never
                                clamped); a float entering widens exactly

    They name C types only -- an extern c fn's parameters and result, a function
    pointer's signature, a pointee, a layout field -- and stay two types
    (Ptr[std::ffi::c::Float] is no Ptr[std::ffi::c::Double]). A float or double
    entering Botlish is a Float64 only when it is finite: a NaN or an infinity
    is NonFiniteFloat (the call, or the layout read, declares it), and negative
    zero is zero. Where a value type is written, std::ffi::c::Double means
    Float64 and std::ffi::c::Float is an error: Botlish has no binary32 number.
    C long double has no type.

    Raw C floating values (intrinsic types of this namespace,
    RAW-C-FLOAT-FFI-MILESTONE-1.md): the same two C types, carried as they are.

      std::ffi::c::RawFloat     C's float, every binary32 bit pattern
      std::ffi::c::RawDouble    C's double, every binary64 bit pattern

    Each has exactly its finite counterpart's C representation (format, size,
    alignment, register class), so a parameter, result, field, element or
    pointee declared raw passes the same machine values -- and every value of
    the format crosses unchanged: NaN of any sign and payload, both infinities,
    negative zero, subnormals. Unlike Float and Double they are types of values
    too, of their own kind, in every position: a raw value is no number. It has
    no arithmetic, ordering, equality or hash (`==` and `hash` refuse it, as
    they refuse a pointer), nothing converts it implicitly, and it needs no
    authority (representing a NaN is no memory access). Between a raw value and
    anything else stand only the explicit operations of the module
    std::ffi::c::raw (stdlib/ffi/c/raw.bot, imported by the programs that use
    them): a raw value from and to its bit pattern, its classification by the
    bits alone, its admission to a Float64 (Float's and Double's own rule:
    NonFiniteFloat for NaN and the infinities, negative zero 0.0) and a
    Float64's narrowing to one (Float's own rounding: to nearest, ties to even,
    an overflow NonFiniteFloat). A raw value's display is its C type and its
    bits: <C float 0x7fc00000>, <C double 0x8000000000000000>.

    Pointers (intrinsic types and operations of this namespace):

      std::ffi::c::Void         the C void: an incomplete pointee, no values
      std::ffi::c::Ptr[T]       a C data pointer whose pointee identity is T:
